* pa-a2-cascode: cascode (CS+CG) power amplifier for gain/headroom at 3.3 V.
* Lineage: 0.18 um cascode PA lineage, e.g. Sowlati & Leenaerts, "A 2.4-GHz
* 0.18-um CMOS self-biased cascode power amplifier", JSSC 2002 family.
* Bench-v1 anchor. Structure-only, ZERO component values.
* Structure: CS NM1 (bottom, input device) stacked under CG NM2 (top,
* cascode) sharing the internal drain node; RF choke L1 feeds the cascode
* drain from VDD; output L-match (series L2 + shunt-C C3) to a DC-blocked
* VOUT1 (C4). Input DC-blocked (C1). Published in-topology BIAS NETWORK:
* current-mirror reference (R1 -> diode NM3) sets the CS gate DC via feed R2;
* the CASCODE gate is divider-biased (R3 VDD->gate, R4 gate->VSS) and
* RF-decoupled to VSS by Cc so it is a clean AC-ground cascode.
* Approved 2026-09-14 (bench round 1, "approve all").
C C1 VIN1 n1
NMOS NM1 n2 n1 VSS VSS
NMOS NM2 n3 n5 n2 VSS
L L1 VDD n3
L L2 n3 n4
C C3 n4 VSS
C C4 n4 VOUT1
R R1 VDD n6
NMOS NM3 n6 n6 VSS VSS
R R2 n6 n1
R R3 VDD n5
R R4 n5 VSS
C Cc n5 VSS
